  "notes": "Complete bounded historical architectural reconstruction: known central sanctuary plus documented cells, meeting hall and common rooms. The sanctuary retains its accepted written niche/court controls. The annex is original estimated architecture: eight cells, ten total rooms, widths, roofs, terracing, positions and finishes are not an excavated plan. Current site ground is coarse modern data and is not a seventh-century bench. Existing sanctuary date650CE and new annex date700CE are retained with broad600–800CE ranges; assembly700CE is illustrative. No image or protected excavation plan used. Story coordinate is approximate and differs by roughly1.4km from the current Wikipedia location; body placement is an approximate site-context visualization, not a surveyed location. The site identity Q42880538 is verified from the Wikipedia Wikidata-item hyperlink; no artifact identity substituted."
